WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.692
Distinguish the framework from the proposal.

2
00:00:02.692 --> 00:00:08.929
Open the Standard Model chart and look at the quarks, leptons, interaction bosons and Higgs.

3
00:00:08.929 --> 00:00:13.259
This is the established particle framework used as a reference in the museum.

4
00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:21.132
BHSM proposes a geometric interpretation and conditionally reproduces the matter and gauge ledger under stated assumptions.

5
00:00:21.132 --> 00:00:24.522
That conditional structural result has a specific scope.

6
00:00:24.522 --> 00:00:32.859
Particle masses, interaction probabilities and cosmological responses each require further physical constructions and independent checks.

7
00:00:32.859 --> 00:00:39.019
The conventional minimal Standard Model also leaves neutrino masses outside its original field content.

8
00:00:39.019 --> 00:00:45.720
Use the exhibit labels to keep established references, conditional results and proposed interpretations distinct.

9
00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:49.934
Ask which parts are measured references and which are BHSM claims.
